{"title":"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The largest number in the list <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/d/6ed474a65e3cb2e61f8f53771c47fce40eba5203.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{\\frac{3}{10}, \\, \\frac{9}{20}, \\, \\frac{12}{25}, \\frac{27}{50}, \\, \\frac{49}{100}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"181\" height=\"38\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4ddb0415c40badd286593aa19e060f59f0bdd344.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ \\frac{3}{10} \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\frac{9}{20} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ \\frac{12}{25} \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\frac{27}{50} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ \\frac{49}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"462\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Expressing the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Element\" title=\"Element\">elements</a> of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">set</a> as decimals gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/0/d0045f4f6c772443b33bed1013afbcae95a4e566.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{0.3, \\, 0.45, \\, 0.48, \\, 0.54, \\, 0.49\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"217\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>The largest of these is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/d/70de634e2950a312db1b1b62f89548d1ac25a27a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.54$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"34\" height=\"14\" />, which is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/5/cc5e7923ed43d719683658ad583ce95491e24046.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } \\frac{27}{50}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"71\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To compare the fractions, we can also express the fractions in terms of the same common denominator, and then see which number has the highest numerator. This gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/5025abeecbd13728ad1dc76296b5f97833014b70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{10} = \\frac{3 \\times 10}{10 \\times 10} = \\frac{30}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"166\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/2630c5ee46f877ea352d41759f68dae794d6e261.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9}{20} = \\frac{9 \\times 5}{20 \\times 5} = \\frac{45}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"157\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/d/59dab0ab4e9a02cfc470f0aa1fd04e46bb866467.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12}{25} = \\frac{12 \\times 4}{25 \\times 4} = \\frac{48}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"157\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/6796cd1d6da0f8e431f9d420e48240f89f8bbaaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{27}{50} = \\frac{27 \\times 2}{50 \\times 2} = \\frac{54}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"157\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90e9f6cfac1e12d9128e8f8f639e7b2359e4d4df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{49}{100} = \\frac{49 \\times 1}{100 \\times 1} = \\frac{49}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"175\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Since the denominators are the same, we can look at the fraction with the highest numerator, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/3/6234e402b44db20c0737079a94b281e4277ee45f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{54}{100} = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } \\frac{27}{50}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"127\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 5\">P